---
// Hero loop: Claude Code proposes a Cai action ("Calm it down"), you approve
// it, then in Slack a rage reply is selected, ⌥C turns it polite, and the
// original lands in Notes. Ends on the ⌥C logo, which is also the first paint
// (the loading state, no poster image needed).
// HTML/CSS instead of a video so copy and UI can change without re-recording.
// Source prototype: cai/_docs/_temp/hero-prototype/index-v3.html (private).
// The review sheet is deliberately simpler than the app's (no shell step, no
// warning or acknowledgment); the Notes list is one note with bullets, while
// the real Save to Notes makes a new note per run.
---

<div class="ha" role="img" aria-label="Demo: an AI agent proposes a Cai action called Calm it down and you approve it. In Slack you select an angry reply, press Option+C, and Cai rewrites it politely in place and saves the original to Notes, running on your Mac with no agent and no tokens.">
    <div class="stage" id="ha-stage" aria-hidden="true">

      <!-- 1. Claude Code proposes the action -->
      <div class="win term fx" id="ha-term">
        <div class="term-bar"><span class="lights"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>Claude Code</span></div>
